WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.523
Cedar Vale Foods buys solar support and battery monitoring from Beacon Grid.

00:04.773 --> 00:06.586
One customer, two services.

00:06.836 --> 00:11.529
Where should each agreement's terms, sales history and billing evidence live in HubSpot?

00:12.200 --> 00:17.896
We'll follow solar support, compare battery monitoring, and build a map you can use on
your own records.

00:18.146 --> 00:20.514
The HubSpot screens show prepared drafts.

00:20.764 --> 00:23.964
The documents are illustrations, not signed agreements.

00:24.633 --> 00:29.540
Solar support runs from November twenty twenty-six through October twenty twenty-seven.

00:29.790 --> 00:32.499
Battery monitoring starts and ends a month later.

00:32.749 --> 00:35.715
Each has its own service scope and renewal decision.

00:36.367 --> 00:39.012
That's why we give them separate agreement identities.

00:39.262 --> 00:41.822
It isn't a rule of one Contract per product.

00:42.072 --> 00:47.213
Services managed under one set of terms can share a Contract with several line items.

00:47.867 --> 00:50.085
The Company identifies the customer.

00:50.335 --> 00:54.837
It cannot, by itself, tell you which service an end date or a price belongs to.

00:55.087 --> 00:57.775
Keep those facts connected to the specific agreement.

00:58.433 --> 01:00.140
Start with the legal evidence.

01:00.390 --> 01:06.001
The master agreement, service schedule and accepted amendments establish what the parties
agreed.

01:06.251 --> 01:10.091
HubSpot's commercial Contract does not replace those documents.

01:10.767 --> 01:14.628
Next, the Deal answers: which sales opportunity are we working on?

01:14.878 --> 01:17.417
Here, the solar draft links to its source Deal.

01:17.667 --> 01:21.912
A future renewal opportunity has a different job from the original sale.

01:22.567 --> 01:26.833
A Quote presents a proposal for buyer acceptance, when that route is used.

01:27.083 --> 01:29.686
Accepted HubSpot quotes can create Contracts.

01:29.936 --> 01:35.163
An agreement signed elsewhere can instead be recorded through the direct-create route,
when available.

01:35.833 --> 01:40.911
The commercial Contract holds the services, term and committed revenue being managed.

01:41.161 --> 01:44.958
This solar example is still a draft, so its values are proposed.

01:45.208 --> 01:48.728
A populated record is not proof of customer acceptance.

01:49.400 --> 01:51.320
The invoice answers what was billed.

01:51.570 --> 01:54.514
The payment record shows payment activity and status.

01:54.764 --> 01:57.409
For this example, HubSpot billing stays off.

01:57.659 --> 02:01.158
We have not created invoices or demonstrated collections.

02:01.833 --> 02:04.031
A Subscription needs one extra check.

02:04.281 --> 02:07.587
In the standard billing flow, it can manage recurring billing.

02:07.837 --> 02:13.320
In HubSpot's connected billing beta, it supports reporting while the Contract controls
billing.

02:13.570 --> 02:17.026
Identify your setup before deciding where to make changes.

02:17.700 --> 02:19.023
Now check the numbers.

02:19.273 --> 02:24.521
The solar line is one thousand US dollars per month, quantity one, for twelve payments.

02:24.771 --> 02:27.736
That gives twelve thousand dollars across this fixed term.

02:28.400 --> 02:30.512
Those numbers describe different measures.

02:30.762 --> 02:33.642
The monthly recurring price is one thousand dollars.

02:33.892 --> 02:35.833
The term total is twelve thousand.

02:36.083 --> 02:39.134
Neither tells you how much has been invoiced or paid.

02:39.800 --> 02:48.035
If a fifteen-hundred-dollar commissioning fee belongs to the same agreement, it adds to
the total commitment, not the recurring monthly price.

02:48.285 --> 02:51.207
If it is separate, leave it outside the solar agreement.

02:51.457 --> 02:55.191
Don't carry a one-time fee into recurring renewal charges.

02:55.867 --> 02:57.787
Always name the field you're comparing.

02:58.037 --> 03:03.029
Deal Amount, recurring value and Contract total can have different calculation rules.

03:03.279 --> 03:06.863
Check the line items and term that produced the displayed number.

03:07.533 --> 03:10.776
Battery monitoring follows the same responsibility map.

03:11.026 --> 03:17.042
It's two hundred and fifty dollars monthly for twelve payments: three thousand dollars
across its term.

03:17.292 --> 03:20.492
Its end date is November thirtieth, twenty twenty-seven.

03:21.167 --> 03:26.841
The customer is shared, but the evidence, terms and next action must point to battery
monitoring.

03:27.091 --> 03:33.385
A link through the same Company is not enough to prove that an invoice or a Deal belongs
to that agreement.

03:34.067 --> 03:37.373
Associations also don't guarantee synchronization.

03:37.623 --> 03:41.634
HubSpot can copy line items into separate record instances.

03:41.884 --> 03:47.473
Compare their values and parent records, rather than assuming one edit updates every
linked record.

03:48.133 --> 03:49.584
Here's the completed map.

03:49.834 --> 03:52.053
The Company identifies the customer.

03:52.303 --> 03:54.223
Documents supply agreed terms.

03:54.473 --> 03:55.987
Deals track opportunities.

03:56.237 --> 03:57.709
Quotes present proposals.

03:57.959 --> 04:00.135
Contracts manage commercial commitments.

04:00.385 --> 04:04.673
Billing records show charges and payment activity, according to your setup.

04:05.333 --> 04:12.203
For each important field, write down its source, the operational record, the responsible
person and when it was checked.

04:12.453 --> 04:17.018
Keep the document reference and relevant clause alongside dates and prices.

04:17.700 --> 04:19.001
Then make three checks.

04:19.251 --> 04:21.619
Can you retrieve the correct agreement evidence?

04:21.869 --> 04:23.661
Do the prices and dates match it?

04:23.911 --> 04:27.047
Do the linked Deal and billing records belong to this agreement?

04:27.297 --> 04:29.772
Record discrepancies and assign an owner.

04:30.433 --> 04:36.471
A shared spreadsheet, controlled document links and assigned HubSpot tasks can support
this manually.

04:36.721 --> 04:45.190
Direct Contract creation has a beta route across plans; quote creation and workflow
automation have separate plan and seat requirements.

04:45.440 --> 04:46.485
Check your account.

04:47.167 --> 04:52.457
Use the accompanying worksheet and matching architecture guide to map one real agreement.

04:52.707 --> 04:58.446
Before automating, know where each fact comes from, which record owns it, and who will
keep it correct.
